{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310749,"nonce":"P72eGps4oikEFwKHArVta3GO+2c=","title":"wasm-codegen bug (OPEN, found 2026-06-21): an inline `if (cond) v = val;` STATEMENT-form reassignment of a loop-local var inside a ...","message":"Found porting the Q8_K activation quantizer to Haxe for the Phase-4 qmatmul ([[project_haxe_q4_dot_phase3]]).\n\nA function with two `for` loops nested (outer s in 0..16, inner j in 0..16) that contains an inline statement-form reassignment of a loop-local var:\n```haxe\nvar q = (v\u003e=0) ? Math.floor(v+0.5) : Math.ceil(v-0.5);\nif (q \u003e 127) q = 127;        // \u003c-- statement-form reassign\nif (q \u003c -128) q = -128;\n```\nmakes the ENTIRE function fail wasmtime compilation: `Error: WASM compilation failed: failed to compile: wasm[0]::function[1356]::Main.f`. Native compiles + runs fine. The generated wasm is invalid (a stack/type imbalance in the SSA→stack lowering for the conditional reassignment in that nested context).\n\n- A absmax loop, B + flat quant loop w/ Math.floor + qs.set, C + nested loops + bsums[s]=sum, D + round-away ternary → ALL COMPILE.\n- E = D + inline `if(q\u003e127)q=127; if(q\u003c-128)q=-128;` → FAILS.\n- F = E but clamp as a ternary expression `(q\u003e127)?127:((q\u003c-128)?-128:q)` (or via an `inline` helper returning the ternary) → COMPILES.\nSo the trigger is specifically the `if (cond) loopVar = const;` statement form (reassigning an existing var) inside the nested loop. Plain `Math.floor`/ternary/`Bytes.set`/`Array[i]=` are all fine.\n\nReplace `if (q\u003e127) q=127; if (q\u003c-128) q=-128;` with `q = (q\u003e127)?127:((q\u003c-128)?-128:q);` (single-assignment ternary). The Q8_K quantizer + qmatmul then compile + run on wasm.\n\nwasm_backend SSA→stack lowering of a conditional that REASSIGNS an existing SSA var (phi merge) inside nested loops — likely a stack-height/type mismatch on the merge block. Repro is /tmp/q4chk/e.hx (fails) vs f.hx (works). General bug: any `if(c) v=k;` reassign pattern in deep loops risks it; preferring ternaries is the safe idiom until fixed.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_wasm_inline_if_reassign_nested_loop` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}